import bisect


def longest_increasing_subsequence(nums):
    tails = []
    for value in nums:
        position = bisect.bisect_left(tails, value)
        if position == len(tails):
            tails.append(value)
        else:
            tails[position] = value
    return len(tails)
```

`tails[k]` holds the smallest possible tail of an increasing subsequence of length `k + 1`, so the answer is `len(tails)` and the running time is O(n log n).

