class MinStack:
    def __init__(self):
        self._data = []
        self._mins = []

    def push(self, value):
        self._data.append(value)
        current = self._mins[-1] if self._mins else value
        self._mins.append(min(value, current))

    def pop(self):
        self._mins.pop()
        return self._data.pop()

    def minimum(self):
        return self._mins[-1]
```

The auxiliary stack stores the running minimum, so `minimum()` is O(1) and every operation stays amortised O(1).
